WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.663 --> 00:00:22.408
you for coming," Monsieur Jondrette said as his wife led Monsieur Leblanc into their apartment.

2
00:00:22.428 --> 00:00:26.491
"Yes, bless you," said Madame Jondrette.

3
00:00:27.012 --> 00:00:31.976
"You have no idea how much we appreciate your helping the Jondrette family."

4
00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:36.750
"Jondrette?" Monsieur Leblanc turned to Monsieur Jondrette in confusion.

5
00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:40.271
"I thought you said your name was Fabantou."

6
00:00:40.291 --> 00:00:43.833
"Fabantou, Jondrette, what does it matter?

7
00:00:44.593 --> 00:00:46.454
As you may recall, I'm an actor.

8
00:00:47.314 --> 00:00:48.895
Jondrette is my stage name.

9
00:00:49.235 --> 00:00:50.396
Now please sit down."

10
00:00:51.576 --> 00:00:55.418
Marius watched as Monsieur Leblanc took a seat in one of his own chairs.

11
00:00:56.638 --> 00:00:59.900
Marius kept his hand still on the pistol in his waistcoat.

12
00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:09.904
"Now I'm wondering, kind sir," Jondrette went on, "if you'd be interested in this valuable painting As Jondrette

13
00:01:09.944 --> 00:01:14.689
began to talk, a man quietly entered the room and took a seat on a bed.

14
00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.092
Leblanc turned around and stared at him.

15
00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:19.493
"Who's that?"

16
00:01:19.513 --> 00:01:22.255
"Oh, he's just one of the neighbors.

17
00:01:22.896 --> 00:01:23.937
Now where was I?

18
00:01:24.297 --> 00:01:25.218
Oh yes, the painting.

19
00:01:25.598 --> 00:01:27.040
Allow me to show it to you."

20
00:01:28.336 --> 00:01:34.079
As Jondrette described the wonders of this work of art, another man slipped quietly into the room.

21
00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:42.304
Again Monsieur Leblanc turned to look at these suspicious characters, and again Monsieur Jondrette reassured him that they

22
00:01:42.324 --> 00:01:43.244
were just neighbors.

23
00:01:44.265 --> 00:01:45.986
Monsieur Leblanc rose to his feet.

24
00:01:46.006 --> 00:01:49.988
"This is an old inn sign worth only a few francs."

25
00:01:51.168 --> 00:01:55.050
Suddenly the door was thrown open and three more thugs entered the room.

26
00:01:56.171 --> 00:02:02.455
One carried an iron club; the second carried a butcher's cleaver; and the third held an enormous key

27
00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.736
stolen from a prison.

28
00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.858
"Is everything ready?"

29
00:02:06.238 --> 00:02:07.359
asked Monsieur Jondrette.

30
00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.282
"Yes, we have the carriages," said the man with the cleaver.

31
00:02:13.183 --> 00:02:15.264
Jondrette suddenly lunged at Leblanc.

32
00:02:15.664 --> 00:02:17.426
"Do you recognize me?"

33
00:02:18.546 --> 00:02:20.428
The older man studied Jondrette.

34
00:02:21.208 --> 00:02:22.789
"No, I don't think so."

35
00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:27.456
"My name is not Fabantou or Jondrette.

36
00:02:27.476 --> 00:02:32.019
My name is Thenardier, and I was the innkeeper at Montfermeil.

37
00:02:32.659 --> 00:02:34.260
Now do you know me?"

38
00:02:35.581 --> 00:02:37.942
Leblanc flushed slightly but stayed calm.

39
00:02:37.962 --> 00:02:40.064
"No more than before."

40
00:02:41.204 --> 00:02:46.647
Thenardier's revelation had little effect on Leblanc, but it completely stunned Marius.

41
00:02:48.488 --> 00:02:50.870
He staggered and almost fell off the table.

42
00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:54.452
Here was the man who had saved his father's life!

43
00:02:55.636 --> 00:02:59.759
Here was the man whom he had been searching for, and this man turned out to be a

44
00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:06.504
criminal! Meanwhile Thenardier was pacing before Leblanc in an insane, frenzied triumph.

45
00:03:06.524 --> 00:03:10.767
"Well, I remember you," he continued.

46
00:03:10.787 --> 00:03:16.451
"One Christmas night you came to my inn and took away Fantine's child, the Lark.

47
00:03:17.492 --> 00:03:22.556
You gave me fifteen hundred francs for that girl, but she was worth much more.

48
00:03:23.532 --> 00:03:27.313
You may dress like a humble man, but I know you're a millionaire."

49
00:03:27.333 --> 00:03:35.315
"I'm not a millionaire," protested Monsieur Leblanc, "and I wouldn't have been mixed up with a crook like

50
00:03:35.375 --> 00:03:37.296
you." "A crook?"

51
00:03:37.636 --> 00:03:38.796
yelped Thenardier.

52
00:03:38.816 --> 00:03:40.917
"I'm a war hero."

53
00:03:41.177 --> 00:03:42.397
He thumped the painting.

54
00:03:42.417 --> 00:03:49.379
"This picture was done by a famous artist, and it shows me rescuing General Pontmercy at the Battle

55
00:03:49.419 --> 00:03:50.159
of Waterloo."

56
00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.040
Marius shuddered.

57
00:03:52.672 --> 00:03:58.874
There was no doubt left; this horrible man was indeed the one who had saved his father.

58
00:03:58.894 --> 00:04:03.696
"It still looks like a sign to me," said Monsieur Leblanc.

59
00:04:05.196 --> 00:04:09.297
"Why, you miserable old—" "Is it time to take care of him now?"

60
00:04:09.618 --> 00:04:11.178
interrupted the man with the club.

61
00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:16.680
Before Thenardier could respond, Monsieur Leblanc jumped up and ran to the window.

62
00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:23.162
He opened it and was halfway out, when three men seized him and wrestled him back into the

63
00:04:23.202 --> 00:04:26.764
room. They threw him onto a bed and tied him up.

64
00:04:28.045 --> 00:04:29.985
Marius watched all this in horror.

65
00:04:30.606 --> 00:04:32.026
Should he fire the pistol?

66
00:04:32.486 --> 00:04:35.488
He wanted to rescue the brave father of the woman he loved.

67
00:04:36.268 --> 00:04:41.530
But if he did that, then the police would arrest Thenardier, who had saved his father's life.

68
00:04:42.531 --> 00:04:45.052
Thenardier sat down on the bed next to Leblanc.

69
00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:48.594
"I think we can come to an understanding.

70
00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:53.096
In a moment we'll untie one hand so you can write a note."

71
00:04:54.317 --> 00:05:01.281
Leblanc remained silent while Madame Thenardier brought a pen and paper, and her husband dictated the following message:

72
00:05:02.481 --> 00:05:04.823
My dear daughter, Come immediately.

73
00:05:05.903 --> 00:05:09.145
The person who gives you this note is instructed to bring you to me.

74
00:05:09.165 --> 00:05:12.387
"Now sign it," said Monsieur Thenardier.

75
00:05:12.407 --> 00:05:14.428
"What's your name anyway?"

76
00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:18.323
"Urbain Fabre," replied Monsieur Leblanc.

77
00:05:19.223 --> 00:05:20.625
Marius stared at the name.

78
00:05:21.505 --> 00:05:24.988
The initials on his precious handkerchief were U.F.

79
00:05:25.929 --> 00:05:29.152
Apparently he'd been wrong to assume it belonged to the daughter.

80
00:05:30.333 --> 00:05:35.377
Thenardier gave the note to his wife, who hurried away with the man carrying the cleaver.

81
00:05:35.397 --> 00:05:40.281
"Now let me explain what's going to happen," said Thenardier.

82
00:05:40.301 --> 00:05:46.074
"My wife will give the note to your daughter, who will accompany her in a carriage.

83
00:05:47.135 --> 00:05:51.638
Somewhere on the edge of the city, the Lark will be transferred to another carriage and taken to

84
00:05:51.678 --> 00:05:53.180
an undisclosed location.

85
00:05:54.100 --> 00:06:00.466
My wife will return here, and as soon as you give me two hundred thousand francs, the Lark

86
00:06:00.946 --> 00:06:01.787
will be released."

87
00:06:03.468 --> 00:06:07.171
Leblanc, whose real name, of course, was Jean Valjean, said nothing.

88
00:06:07.191 --> 00:06:14.982
"By the way," said Thenardier, "if you have me arrested, my friend will take care of the Lark,

89
00:06:15.342 --> 00:06:16.463
if you know what I mean.

90
00:06:17.444 --> 00:06:19.185
Her fate is in your hands."

91
00:06:20.586 --> 00:06:21.747
Marius was in shock.

92
00:06:22.328 --> 00:06:26.811
These hoodlums were kidnapping his beloved, but they weren't bringing her back here?

93
00:06:27.792 --> 00:06:29.954
One of them was going to carry her off and harm her?

94
00:06:31.055 --> 00:06:34.017
He wanted to fire the pistol, but what good would it do?

95
00:06:34.617 --> 00:06:37.660
The hideous man with the cleaver would still have the Lark.

96
00:06:38.668 --> 00:06:42.850
Suddenly he heard the door slam downstairs and someone running up the stairs.

97
00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:47.992
Madame Thenardier burst into her apartment, followed by the man with the cleaver.

98
00:06:48.012 --> 00:06:49.993
"False address!"

99
00:06:50.533 --> 00:06:51.553
she said breathlessly.

100
00:06:51.573 --> 00:06:55.455
"No one at that place had ever heard of Urbain Fabre!"

101
00:06:56.896 --> 00:07:00.697
Marius breathed a sigh of relief because the Lark was safe.

102
00:07:00.717 --> 00:07:03.198
"A false address!"

103
00:07:03.678 --> 00:07:05.179
exclaimed Monsieur Thenardier.

104
00:07:05.199 --> 00:07:07.340
"What did you hope to gain by that?"

105
00:07:08.284 --> 00:07:09.785
"Time!" said Valjean.

106
00:07:10.285 --> 00:07:14.227
At that moment he shook off the ropes, which he had somehow managed to cut.

107
00:07:15.108 --> 00:07:19.250
Fastened by only one leg to the bed, he reached for the chisel in the fire.

108
00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:23.352
He pressed it to his forearm as the others recoiled in horror.

109
00:07:23.372 --> 00:07:26.514
"Do to me what you will," he said.

110
00:07:26.534 --> 00:07:28.115
"I'm not afraid."

111
00:07:28.135 --> 00:07:34.438
"It's time to kill him," muttered Madame Thenardier as her husband reached for the carving knife in the

112
00:07:34.478 --> 00:07:37.780
drawer. Marius looked wildly about him.

113
00:07:38.344 --> 00:07:40.245
Was now the moment to fire the pistol?

114
00:07:40.765 --> 00:07:41.806
But what about the Lark?

115
00:07:42.506 --> 00:07:44.968
Suddenly he spotted a piece of paper on his table.

116
00:07:45.608 --> 00:07:47.589
It said, "The cops are here."

117
00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:52.572
He wrapped it around a piece of plaster and tossed it through the hole in the wall.

118
00:07:52.592 --> 00:07:54.113
"What was that?"

119
00:07:54.513 --> 00:07:55.754
cried Madame Thenardier.

120
00:07:55.774 --> 00:07:58.295
"Look!" said her husband.

121
00:07:58.315 --> 00:08:00.016
"It's Eponine's writing.

122
00:08:00.396 --> 00:08:02.357
She must have thrown it through the window to warn us."

123
00:08:03.338 --> 00:08:07.040
The thug with the enormous key tossed it on the floor and signaled the others.

124
00:08:07.656 --> 00:08:09.278
"It's time to get out of here!"

125
00:08:10.258 --> 00:08:14.302
Quickly another thug unrolled the rope ladder and attached it to the window.

126
00:08:14.322 --> 00:08:16.464
"Not so fast!"

127
00:08:16.864 --> 00:08:17.965
said a voice at the door.

128
00:08:18.866 --> 00:08:22.008
To Marius' relief, it belonged to Javert.

129
00:08:22.649 --> 00:08:26.632
A squad of policemen rushed into the room and handcuffed the thugs.

130
00:08:26.652 --> 00:08:29.815
"Now where is that man you were holding hostage?"

131
00:08:30.275 --> 00:08:31.036
asked Javert.

132
00:08:31.976 --> 00:08:35.900
An officer ran to the window, where the rope ladder was still trembling.

133
00:08:36.597 --> 00:08:38.182
"He seems to have escaped, sir."
